**Q3) Calculate the claim cost to premium ratio for each policy tenure.**
**SQL Query**

SELECT 
    p.Policy_Tenure,
    SUM(c.Claim_Amount) AS Total_Claims,
    SUM(p.Premium) AS Total_Premium,
    SUM(c.Claim_Amount) / SUM(p.Premium) AS Claim_Premium_Ratio
FROM policy_sales_data p
LEFT JOIN claims_data c
ON p.Customer_ID = c.Customer_ID
GROUP BY p.Policy_Tenure
ORDER BY p.Policy_Tenure;

**ANSWER**
| Tenure | Claims      | Premium     | Ratio    |
| ------ | ----------- | ----------- | -------- |
| 1 year | 78,650,000  | 20,000,000  | **3.93** |
| 2 year | 117,650,000 | 60,000,000  | **1.96** |
| 3 year | 158,250,000 | 120,000,000 | **1.32** |
| 4 year | 138,890,000 | 40,000,000  | **3.47** |

**3 year tenure is most profitable**

